        "id": 1366,
        "relationship_type": "misc",
        "body": "い-Adjectives describe the state or characteristics of nouns and can be used at the end of a sentence or directly before a noun. For example, 面白い本 means 'an interesting book.' Similarly, Japanese verbs, unlike English verbs, can also modify nouns. For example, 読んだ本 means 'the book [I] read.'",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 357,
