      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 1367,
        "relationship_type": "misc",
        "body": "な-Adjectives describe the state or characteristics of nouns. They can be used at the end of a sentence (followed by だ or です) or precede a noun with な. For example, 大変な仕事 means 'a tough job.' Similarly, Japanese verbs can modify nouns directly, unlike な-Adjectives. For example, 読んだ本 means 'the book (I) read.'",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 357,
          "slug": "verb-た-noun",
