      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 1363,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "The ている① form expresses completed actions or past states. Unlike English, verbs can directly modify nouns, similar to い-Adjectives. For example, 読んでいる本 means 'the book [I] am reading.' However, when describing a noun's state, the past form (た) is often preferred over ている. For example, 死んだネズミ ('a dead mouse') is more common than 死んでいるネズミ.",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 357,
          "slug": "verb-た-noun",
          "title": "Verb［た・ている］+ Noun",
          "meaning": "Verb modified noun, Relative clause",
          "level": "JLPT5",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
          "type_snake": "grammar_point"
        },
        "second_relatable": {
          "id": 27,
